refusedCondT -- F-147, SEQ 556 (Tony, 2026-11-07): a refused condition or value crashed the new road's build at exit 139. Rows prefixed RC-.

Not run alone: pop.sh builds each row, everything above this stop(); then the row, a statement that must still run, then a sentinel. The
adjacent run `qa qb + 1` is the child: EXPRESSIOn refuses it by name and clears its label, so the parent's `**EXPRESSIOn` reads null and the
parent attaches it. Each row reads, by value: exit 0; the child's refusal; the attach's refusal, naming the list the rule was building; and
the next statement's output. The cure is in one place (R1): opAddAttribute refuses a null attach, so the rows are one per shape and no rule
carries a guard. Roots first, then the four shapes through STARt, the road a program takes.

